{title: 308 - Wholly Thine}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]I would be, dear Savior, wholly Thine; Teach me how, teach me how;
[G]I would do Thy will, O Lord, not mine; Help [D7]me, help me now.
[G]Wholly Thine, wholly Thine, Wholly [D]Thine, this is my vow;
[G/D]Wholly Thine, wholly Thine, Wholly [D7]Thine, OLord, just now.

Refrain:
[D7]Wholly Thine, wholly Thine,
[G/D]Wholly Thine, this is my vow;
[D7]Wholly Thine, wholly Thine,
[G]Wholly Thine, O Lord, just now.

Verse 2:
[G]What is worldly pleasure, wealth or fame,
[G]Without Thee, without [D7]Thee?
[G]I will leave them all [D]for Thy dear Name,
[G/D]This my wealth [D7]shall be.

Verse 3:
[G]As I cast earth's transient joys behind,
[G]Come Thou near, come [D7]Thou near;
[G]In Thy presence all [D]in all I find,
[G/D]'Tis my comfort [D7]here.
